  "title": "Outgoing-only joint voter rejects a valid recovery snapshot",
  "cause": "The live snapshot recipient check searches only incoming voters and current learners, omitting outgoing voters and staged learners that are full members of a joint ConfState.",
  "trigger": "A follower that is represented only in VotersOutgoing falls behind a leader that snapshots and compacts through the joint-configuration entry, then receives the newer joint snapshot.",
  "consequence": "The follower repeatedly rejects its only compacted recovery state and remains unable to catch up; when it is needed for the outgoing majority, joint-consensus progress is unavailable.",
  "sites": [
    "raft.go:restore"
  ],
  "actions": [
    "ProtocolReceive"
  ],
  "invariants": [
    "JointSnapshotMemberAcceptance"
  ],
  "premises": [
    "The snapshot index is newer than the receiver's committed index.",
    "The receiver is a follower and is a legitimate member solely through VotersOutgoing.",
    "The leader has compacted the preceding log, so snapshot installation is the recovery path.",
    "No transport or caller guard removes a valid outgoing-only voter from the joint ConfState."
  ],
